Krypton level 3 -> 4
====================
We intercepted "krypton4.enc" (hex encoded). It was encrypted by XOR-ing the
plaintext with a short secret key that is repeated over and over.

Our agents report that every transmission begins with the header:

    KRYPTON TRANSMISSION

ciphertext XOR plaintext = key.  Recover the key, then decrypt everything.

Hints:
  xxd -r -p krypton4.enc | xxd        # view the raw bytes
  python3: bytes.fromhex(...), a ^ b, and the % operator for repeating keys.
  The key is shorter than the header - look for the point where it repeats.

